  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1255 AM Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Dry air, clear skies, and light winds tonight over \nthe Piedmont will lead to lows in the lower to mid 40s. It will be a \nbit warmer in the Coastal Plain where the northerly wind will remain \nup around 5-12 mph overnight as low pressure strengthens well off \nthe mid-Atlantic coast. \n\nAs low pressure strengthens off the mid-Atlantic coast today and \ntonight and moves slowly north, strong dry and cool advection will \nallow the dew points to fall into the mid 30s to lower 40s over the \nW-NW Piedmont this afternoon into tonight. Expect mostly sunny skies \ntoday with highs generally 70-73 with a gusty N wind at 15-20 mph \nwith gusts to 25-30 mph. The stronger winds (up to 35 mph) are \nexpected in the Coastal Plain. These highs will be 5-10 degrees \nbelow normal. \n\nThe lows tonight will be the coolest since May with readings in the \n40-45 range in the Piedmont, and generally 15 to 20 degrees below \nnormal. This will be due to the very dry air, diminishing wind to \nlight, and clear skies. The lows tonight should be 5-10 degrees \nwarmer in the Coastal Plain where the surface and boundary layer \nwill remain mixed keeping the north wind stirring. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Excellent weather for the upcoming weekend across \nour region with temperatures very close to normal by day - and a bit \non the cool side by night. \n\nMostly sunny skies are expected this weekend; however, the skies may \nbecome partly sunny at times in the NE Saturday due to some \ncloudiness from the low pressure off the mid-Atlantic and New \nEngland coast that will be moving very slowly. Highs will recover \ninto the mid 70s to lower 80s Saturday and mostly in the lower 80s \nSunday. Overnight lows will be in the 40s west and lower 50s east \nwith mainly clear skies. These lows will again be well below normal \nthrough the weekend (by 10-15 degrees).\n\nThe next chance of showers may hold off until the end of the \nupcoming work week as high pressure dominates the SE states through \nat least Thursday. Lows will moderate into the 50s mid-week then 60s \nlate week. Highs will generally be in the 80s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3... Dry and becoming seasonably warm most of the week. \nThe next chance of showers holds off until very late in the week.\n\nThe next chance of showers will likely hold off until Friday as an \nupper level ridge is forecast to strengthen over the SE states well \ninto the upcoming week (and possibly into next weekend). \nTemperatures will return to above normal levels especially Thursday \nand beyond.",
